\details{
The user inputs for this module are separated from the outputs to allow for
more flexible UI design.

This module wraps \code{\link[dittoSeq:dittoDotPlot]{dittoSeq::dittoDotPlot()}}, the standard marker figure: for
each gene (or numeric metadata) and group, a dot whose colour is the mean
expression of the cells expressing it and whose size is the fraction of cells
expressing it. The resulting \code{ggplot} is converted to an interactive \code{plotly}
figure. \code{ggplotly()} drops ggplot's size legend, so the dot-size legend is
redrawn with \code{\link[VizModules:add_size_legend]{VizModules::add_size_legend()}}, as the VizModules DotPlot
module draws its own: circles sized from the plotted dots, labelled with the
percentage of cells expressing.
}
